Controller public diagnostic boundary
====================================

ControllerResponse/ControllerWithStats and the metadata sync response project
last_error and error_history through a fixed local diagnostic vocabulary.
Unknown legacy/provider text becomes a generic category, not a pattern-based
redaction. History contains at most ten valid bounded timestamps and safe error
labels. Arbitrary historical extra fields are not returned. Projection copies
the response and does not rewrite controller configuration or legacy DB records.
Existing credential-key redaction and tenant/site authorization remain in place.

Saved and precreation connection tests preserve success/failure and ordinary
controller details but do not echo provider message/error strings. Successful
responses clear the public error. Failed responses and newly persisted last_error
use fixed diagnostics. Initial background connection checks use the same safe
boundary. Saved/precreation site-probe handlers log fixed failure categories and
use type-based hints. Proxmox unknown responses expose only a validated integer
HTTP status in 100..599; exception text and untyped status values are not copied.
Connectivity guidance refers to trusted TLS configuration rather than disabling
certificate verification.

The documented scope is diagnostic fields and these connection/site-probe
handlers. This is not recursive sanitization of arbitrary provider data, version,
name or runtime/configuration payloads. Existing untouched DB diagnostic bytes
remain sensitive until a separate retention/migration policy removes them.
Other controller operations, infrastructure/Celery logs and asynchronous errors
outside the adapter-handling block require separate review. This change does not
add execution-time authorization fencing to initial background connection work.

Qualification uses real PostgreSQL and HTTP-ASGI response serialization, including
committed background connection tests. Authentication context, adapters and the
creation quota check are synthetic; no hardware or external notification/broker
publication is performed. Read-only projection preserves exact stored errors,
config and update timestamps. Foreign-tenant/site denials remain compatibility
controls, and known authentication hints are retained.
